# Response headers for the browser build.
#
# This is the Cloudflare Pages / Netlify `_headers` format. It has to sit in the
# *published* directory, so it lives in web/ and `flutter build web` copies it
# to build/web alongside everything else. Vercel does not read this file — see
# vercel.json at the repository root.
#
# Cross-origin isolation is what lets Chrome and Safari put the database in the
# origin-private file system instead of IndexedDB. It is an optimisation, not a
# requirement: without these headers drift falls back to IndexedDB in a shared
# worker, which is durable and safe across tabs, just slower. See
# docs/web-build.md.
#
# It is safe to enable here only because the page loads nothing cross-origin —
# `--no-web-resources-cdn` keeps the engine on this origin. Adding a remote
# script or font later means removing these headers or the page will not load
# at all.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
